  "notes": "Piano solo on ONE grand staff (brace). A correct conversion yields exactly ONE part \"Piano\" with 2 staves; it must NOT be split into right/left hand parts, and the second right-hand voice in bars 13-16 must stay inside the piano part (voice 2), not become a new part. DAMAGE (photocopy-thick): Dark photocopy, 1-bit: high threshold + ink spread - noteheads fill in (half notes start to look like quarters), beams/slurs/ties merge with staff lines, lyrics thicken. scan adds toner specks and a black lid edge; severe adds -1.2 deg skew, black surround, heavy specks and pepper noise. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Severe: some hollow (half/whole) noteheads may be visually filled; durations remain as in the truth (they are recoverable from beat counting only)."
